{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_019Xh6DtLBx4J6rjUHGs4YPo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchor is a **personal productivity + R&D mission-control system** built for one user (J.C. Liechty), living entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor`. Grounded claims:\n\n**Purpose**\n- It's a single-user task/project manager whose **source of truth is plain markdown** (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`, plus `CANCELLED.md`/`SAVED_FOR_LATER.md` archives) â€” no database, no syncing, one folder.\n- It manages a full **task lifecycle**: Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled â†’ Saved-for-Later â†’ Restored, with optional Notes per task.\n\n**What it does / ships**\n- **`anchor_gui.py`** â€” the primary app and the one declared deliverable: a stdlib-only Python HTTP server that renders the whole dashboard, reads/writes the markdown directly, and runs persistently as the NSSM Windows service **`anchor`** on `http://localhost:8777`.\n- **`anchor.py`** â€” a CLI engine mirroring the same logic (done/add/capture/cancel/save/restore) and generating static `dashboard.html`.\n- **`anchor_healthcheck.py`** â€” a daily 5 AM self-test (Task Scheduler) that parses every file, exercises every endpoint, walks a synthetic task through all states, and writes `health_reports/`.\n\n**The R&D \"cockpit\" layer (the bulk of recent work)**\n- Beyond plain tasks, Anchor became a **mission-control for \"trio\"-driven R&D projects** â€” the trio being researchPrime (research) â†’ Crucible (planning) â†’ Foreman (build).\n- Each project gets a window where **lanes (Research Â· Planning Â· Build Â· Deliverables Â· Grass Catchers)** show their most-recent session as a **status-lit tile** (green/amber/red/grey) that **expands an inline panel** with a cached summary on top and a **real, resizable terminal below**.\n- It ships **real ConPTY terminals** (the one declared native exception, `pywinpty`, lazily imported in `pty_manager.py` only), **per-session git-worktree isolation**, an **engine toggle** (Claude â†” Gemini, Gemini research-only), **proactive cached summaries**, **per-lane doc-role maps**, **cost/tokens/time rollups**, and **type-aware deliverable launching** (skill/tool verify Â· service preview on a port â‰  8777 Â· program run Â· doc render).\n- This is now at **v4 \"Project Cockpit\"** â€” built by Foreman (9 waves green, 637 tests passing) and merged to `master` (commit `38fd70e`), succeeding the earlier v2 and v3 \"Mission Control\" surfaces.\n\n**Branding:** it's presented as a **Ghost World Labs** tool \"Powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢,\" using a vendored brand mark.\n\nOne honest caveat: the docs say v4 is built/merged and deployed via `nssm restart anchor` â€” I'm reporting that status as written in `CLAUDE.md`/memory, not from independently re-running the test suite this session."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45311,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d5c3be4f-be0f-46df-886f-a6f67e393341","uuid":"c100a92a-1f4d-452f-bfcb-3451a617b2cc","request_id":"req_011Cc1JRLTeLcvgk8La6GvbC"}
